{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#full-time-speech-language-pathology-assistant-professor": {
      "title": "Full-Time: Speech Language Pathology, Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Full-Time: Speech Language Pathology, Assistant Professor. DeSales University invites applications for a full-time, 9-month tenure-track faculty position in our Communication Sciences & Disorders Department. Rank will be commensurate with experience and accomplishment. We value innovative and evidence-based instruction, interprofessional training, community engagement, and culturally responsive practice. Along with dedicated classroom and clinical laboratory space in our recently renovated Wills Hall, the Speech Language Pathology (SLP) program shares classrooms, a human gross anatomy laboratory, and a state-of-the-art Simulation Center with students in our nationally recognized nursing, physical therapy, and physician assistant science programs. The SLP program hosts the University Speech Clinic providing treatment for underserved populations across diagnoses, the lifespan, and the diversity of backgrounds in our community. With differentiated tracts and a global mindset, we have significant impact on the greater Lehigh Valley community, student learning, and faculty growth and contribution to the field. The program offers undergraduate majors (3+2 accelerated, traditional 4-year) and the degree of Master of Science in Speech-Language Pathology. The graduate program prepares students for entry level practice as speech-language pathologists with the opportunity to gain clinical experience across a range of settings including our own on-campus Clinic. Job Description Qualifications include a doctorate (PhD, EdD, CScD) (ABD considered), CCC-SLP or eligibility, evidence of research activity, and commitment to effective classroom teaching. We are specifically seeking applicants with expertise in the following areas: Dysphagia Head and neck cancer Voice Motor speech disorders This position is accountable for the following: Teaching, scholarship and service responsibilities consistent with university expectations for full-time faculty members Teaching core curriculum and other courses based on areas of content knowledge and when appropriate supervising students within areas of clinical expertise in the University Speech & Hearing Clinic Understanding the needs of a student population of great diversity – in age, cultural background, ethnicity, primary language and academic preparation – through inclusive course materials, teaching strategies and advisement Providing effective, ongoing communication with clinical educators and students while monitoring and documenting the academic performance of students to assure that they successfully achieve the outcomes for completing the program Establishing and maintaining a plan for self-development that includes participation in and enhancement of teaching and development of scholarly activities consistent with the SLP program, CAA, and University expectations All faculty members at DeSales are expected to contribute to university, division and program level service, including student advisement, scholarly activity and professional development, and support the university, college, and program’s missions and visions and advance the strategic plan. Minimum Requirements: Doctorate in relevant field (ABD may be considered) Knowledge of communication disorders across the lifespan Strong communication, organization, interpersonal, problem-solving, and counseling skills An awareness of and sensitivity to the educational goals of a multicultural population as might have been gained in cross-cultural study, training, teaching and other comparable experience Preferred Requirements PhD (ABD may be considered) Pennsylvania licensure (or eligible) in Speech-Language Pathology Prior teaching experience at the graduate level with demonstrated understanding of adult learning theory and principles Membership in the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association (ASHA) is highly valued Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Qualified applicants should submit electronically a cover letter outlining interest in and qualifications for the position, a curriculum vitae, statement of clinical practice and teaching, three professional letters of recommendation, and photocopies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required, if hired) to the Program Director, Dr. Susy Keller at Susana.Keller@desales.edu. In the subject line of the email, please only include your Last Name - SLP Faculty . DeSales University is an EEO employer - M/F/Vets/Disabled; Applicants must be authorized to work in the U.S. This position is not eligible for immigration sponsorship."
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#full-time-assistant-professor-chemistry": {
      "title": "Full-Time: Assistant Professor, Chemistry",
      "description": "Full-Time: Assistant Professor, Chemistry. DeSales University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Chemistry at the Assistant Professor level, beginning Fall 2027. We seek a collaborative educator-scholar with expertise in analytical chemistry and instrumentation who is committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, mentoring, science outreach, and to the development of a sustained undergraduate research program. The successful candidate will contribute to a department focused on student-centered learning, hands-on scientific training, and undergraduate research. Responsibilities Teach undergraduate courses in general and analytical chemistry as well as instrumental analysis, including laboratories Develop, maintain, and actively use shared instrumentation resources in both teaching and research Establish a productive undergraduate research program, mentoring and involving students in independent and course-based research Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, student advisement and departmental initiatives Engage in service to the department, university, and broader community Participate in faculty development opportunities and attend conferences Requirements Ph.D. in Chemistry or closely related field Demonstrated expertise in analytical chemistry and chemical instrumentation Strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentoring Clear ability and commitment to developing and sustaining an undergraduate research program Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching at the undergraduate level Experience maintaining, troubleshooting, or managing instrumentation Experience mentoring undergraduate students in research Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate STEM education and outreach Additional Information : Start Date: August 2027 with option to begin January 2027 To apply, please submit electronically (PDF preferred) the following material to Dr. Steve Sweeney, Department Chair of Chemistry & Biochemistry at steven.sweeney@desales.edu . In the subject line of the email, please only include your Last Name- Chemistry Faculty Position : Letter of Application (outlining interest and qualifications) Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Statement (describing how you would engage undergraduate students in your scholarly efforts) Contact Information for three Professional References Photocopies of all Transcripts (official transcripts will be required, if hired) Priority review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration; however, the position will remain open until filled. Applications must be complete to be considered for review. The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry is located in the Priscilla Payne Hurd Science Center. Our facilities are well-equipped with state-of-the-art instrumentation supported by college-controlled endowments. Instrumentation includes a 60-MHz teaching NMR spectrometer, thermal analysis (STA, bomb calorimetry), UV-Vis and fluorescence spectrophotometers, multiple UV-Vis and IR spectrometers, a magnetic susceptibility balance, as well as other chromatographic (GC-TCD, GC-MS with FID and headspace sampler, HPLC, FPLC), electrochemical, and biochemical instrumentation. University endowment funds are available to provide start-up support for new faculty and continued support for research endeavors. DeSales University is an EEO employer - M/F/Vets/Disabled; Applicants must be authorized to work in the U.S. This position is not eligible for immigration sponsorship."
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#full-time-assistant-professor-biology": {
      "title": "Full-Time: Assistant Professor, Biology",
      "description": "Full-Time: Assistant Professor, Biology. The Department of Biology and Neuroscience in the College of Sciences at DeSales University invites applications for a full-time position in biology at the assistant professor rank (tenure-track) or assistant professor of practice rank (non-tenure track) with expertise in human anatomy and physiology to begin August 2027. The successful candidate will hold a Ph.D. (or ABD) in Human Anatomy, Human Physiology, or a related field, or possess a terminal clinical or allied health degree by the time of appointment. Teaching expectations include contributing to our current offerings in anatomy and physiology (lecture and labs), as well as contributing to our biology curriculum and developing courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Additionally, tenure-track faculty are expected to develop an active research program that will include undergraduate students. Professor of practice faculty are expected to remain current in their respective field through participation in scholarly activity reflective of their degree. Salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience and training. The position will report to the Department Chair of Biology and Neuroscience. The Department of Biology and Neuroscience is located in the Priscilla Payne Hurd Science Center and Campbell Hall. Our facilities are well-equipped for cell/tissue culture, fluorescence microscopy, small animal, molecular biology/genetics, microbiology, and neuroscience research. Our Gambet Center for Business and Healthcare houses a gross anatomy lab. University endowment funds are available to provide start-up support for new faculty and continued support for research endeavors. To apply, please submit electronically (PDF preferred) the following materials to Dr. Joshua Slee, Department Chair of Biology at Biology@desales.edu . In the subject line of the email, please only include your Last Name- Biology Faculty Position : Letter of Application (outlining interest and qualifications) Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Contact Information for three Professional References Photocopies of all Transcripts (official transcripts will be required, if hired) Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications must be complete to be considered for review. DeSales University is an EEO employer - M/F/Vets/Disabled; Applicants must be authorized to work in the U.S. This position is not eligible for immigration sponsorship."
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#associate-dean-school-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, School of Nursing",
      "description": "Associate Dean, School of Nursing. DeSales University invites applications for the position of Associate Dean for the School of Nursing. This is a 12-month administrative faculty position reporting directly to the Dean of the College of Healthcare Professions. The Associate Dean functions as the Chief Nursing Administrator (CNA) in accordance with the Pennsylvania State Board of Nursing regulations. The Associate Dean provides leadership for all undergraduate and graduate nursing programs, including pre-licensure, master's, doctoral, and post-graduate certificate in advanced practice nursing programs. The successful candidate will provide visionary leadership to advance the School of Nursing's mission of preparing highly competent, compassionate, and ethical nursing professionals grounded in the Catholic, Salesian values of DeSales University. The Associate Dean will collaborate closely with faculty, students, healthcare partners, and university leadership to promote academic excellence, innovation, enrollment growth, regulatory compliance, and student success. Position Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Administration Provide strategic vision and leadership for the School of Nursing consistent with the mission and strategic priorities of DeSales University and the College of Healthcare Professions. Serve as the primary liaison to the Pennsylvania State Board of Nursing and nursing accrediting agencies. Lead strategic planning, program development, enrollment growth initiatives, and continuous quality improvement efforts. Foster a culture of collaboration, accountability, innovation, inclusivity, and academic excellence. Represent the School of Nursing within the University and with external healthcare, academic, and professional organizations. Collaborate with healthcare partners to expand clinical education opportunities, workforce development initiatives, and academic-practice Academic Program Leadership Provide oversight for all undergraduate and graduate nursing programs. Ensure program quality, curricular integrity, and alignment with professional standards and healthcare workforce needs. Lead curriculum review, assessment, revision, and program evaluation activities. Support the development and implementation of innovative educational models, including simulation, hybrid, online, and competency-based learning approaches. Facilitate the development of new academic programs and certificates to meet evolving healthcare demands. Accreditation and Regulatory Compliance Maintain compliance with all Pennsylvania State Board of Nursing regulations. Ensure ongoing compliance with Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) and Council on Accreditation of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs (COA-NAEP) accreditation standards. Lead accreditation self-studies, annual reports, substantive change submissions, site visits, and quality improvement initiatives. Monitor key program outcomes including licensure pass rates, certification examination outcomes, retention, progression, graduation, employment, and student satisfaction metrics. Faculty Leadership and Development Recruit, mentor, develop, evaluate, and retain highly qualified nursing faculty and staff. Promote faculty excellence in teaching, scholarship, service, and professional practice. Oversee faculty workload assignments, annual evaluations, promotion, tenure, and professional development processes. Encourage interprofessional collaboration among programs within the College of Healthcare Professions. Support faculty engagement in scholarly activities, grant development, community partnerships, and professional organizations. Student Success and Enrollment Management Collaborate with admissions, enrollment management, marketing, and student affairs to achieve enrollment and retention goals. Support initiatives that enhance student engagement, academic success, licensure outcomes, and career readiness. Address student concerns and facilitate effective resolution of academic and professional issues. Promote a student-centered environment that values professionalism, diversity, belonging, and service. Clinical Partnerships and Workforce Development Develop and strengthen relationships with regional healthcare organizations, clinical agencies, and community partners. Collaborate with healthcare systems to expand clinical placements, residency partnerships, workforce initiatives, and continuing education opportunities. Support innovative partnerships that advance healthcare education and community health. Budget and Resource Management Develop and manage the School of Nursing operating budget in collaboration with the Dean. Monitor personnel, operational, and capital expenditures. Identify opportunities for external funding, grants, philanthropic support, and strategic partnerships. Ensure efficient allocation of resources to support academic excellence and program growth. Scholarship and Service Maintain an active program of scholarship and professional engagement appropriate to faculty rank. Contribute to university governance and strategic initiatives. Represent DeSales University through service to professional organizations and the broader healthcare community. Required Qualifications Earned master's degree in nursing from an accredited institution. Earned doctoral degree in nursing or related field (PhD, EdD, DNP) by the time of appointment. Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license or eligibility for licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Minimum of five years of progressive leadership experience in nursing education/nursing service. Demonstrated success in academic administration, faculty leadership, accreditation, assessment, and regulatory compliance. Experience teaching in undergraduate and/or graduate nursing programs. Strong understanding of nursing education trends, healthcare workforce needs, and contemporary issues affecting nursing education. Excellent communication, organizational, interpersonal, and leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience serving as a Chief Nursing Administrator, Associate Dean, Dean, Director, Department Chair, or Program Director. Experience overseeing multiple nursing programs and educational modalities. Experience with CCNE accreditation processes and Pennsylvania Board of Nursing regulations. Experience managing budgets, personnel, strategic planning, and enrollment initiatives. Record of scholarly achievement and professional leadership. Experience supporting doctoral and advanced practice nursing education. Salary and Benefits Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. DeSales University offers a comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, vision, retirement contributions, tuition remission, and professional development support. Application Process Applications will be reviewed and accepted until the position is filled. Please submit a cover letter outlining your interest in and qualification for the position, curriculum vitae , statement of leadership philosophy and vision for the future of nursing education, three professional letters of reference, and photocopies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired) to: Leo-Felix M, Jurado , PhD, RN, APN, NE-BC, CNE, ANEF, FAAN Inaugural Dean & Professor, College of Healthcare Professions DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034-9568 Electronic submissions should be emailed to Leo.Jurado@desales.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#full-time-nursing": {
      "title": "Full-Time: Nursing",
      "description": "Full-Time: Nursing. DeSales University School of Nursing invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track or clinical faculty Assistant Professor to begin in Fall 2026. The faculty member hired for this 12-month, full-time, position is mainly responsible for teaching students in the undergraduate and graduate nursing courses in classroom, laboratory, clinical, hybrid, and online formats. The role also includes student advising and recruitment responsibilities. The successful candidate will contribute to the education of future nursing professionals through excellence in teaching, scholarship, service, and student mentorship. The successful candidate is expected to support the mission and values of the university while fostering a student-centered learning environment that promotes academic excellence, clinical competence, and professional leadership. Required qualification Earned master's degree in nursing from an accredited institution. Earned doctoral degree in nursing or related field (PhD, EdD, DNP) by the time of appointment. Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license or eligibility for licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Minimum of five years of clinical nursing experience. Preferred qualification Previous teaching experience in higher education. Experience with simulation-based education and clinical instruction. National specialty certification in an area of nursing practice. Experience with online and hybrid course delivery. Evidence of scholarship through research, publications, presentations, or other scholarly activities. Experience with curriculum development, assessment, or accreditation processes. Applications will be reviewed immediately and accepted until the position is filled. Please submit a cover letter outlining your interest in and qualification for the position, curriculum vitae , three professional letters of reference, and photocopies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired) to: Dr. Leo-Felix M. Jurado College of Healthcare Professions, School of Nursing DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034-9568 Electronic submissions should be emailed to Leo.Jurado@desales.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-adult-studies-multiple-disciplines-needed": {
      "title": "Adjunct: Adult Studies — Multiple Disciplines Needed",
      "description": "Adjunct: Adult Studies — Multiple Disciplines Needed. The Adult Studies program seeks to maintain a qualified faculty pool for the following disciplines: Accounting (financial accounting, managerial accounting, federal income taxation, corporate financial reporting, and regulation) Healthcare Administration Information Technology Psychology (social psychology, psychobiology, human development, counseling psychology, research design and analysis) Teaching formats are online and on-campus/hybrid courses. A Master's degree in the appropriate discipline is required; teaching experience using technology (Brightspace) preferred. Please send resumes to: Lauren.Sherman@desales.edu"
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-biology": {
      "title": "Adjunct: Biology",
      "description": "Adjunct: Biology. The Department of Biology at DeSales University seeks to maintain a qualified applicant pool for adjunct faculty to teach Biology lecture and laboratory courses as needed. Courses include General Biology, Anatomy and Physiology, Molecular and Cell Biology, Immunology and Microbiology. M.S. in Biology is a minimum requirement. Interested applicants should send a cover letter and C.V. to NaturalScience@desales.edu . Or Ms. Laura Stevens Department of Natural Science DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034"
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-chemistry": {
      "title": "Adjunct: Chemistry",
      "description": "Adjunct: Chemistry. The Department of Chemistry and Physics at DeSales University seeks to maintain a qualified applicant pool for adjunct faculty to teach Chemistry lecture and laboratory courses as needed. Courses include General Chemistry, Physiological Chemistry, or Organic Chemistry. M.S. in Chemistry or related field is a minimum requirement. Interested applicants should send a cover letter and C.V. to NaturalScience@desales.edu . Or Ms. Laura Stevens Department of Natural Science DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034"
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-communication-sciences-disorders": {
      "title": "Adjunct: Communication Sciences & Disorders",
      "description": "Adjunct: Communication Sciences & Disorders. DeSales University’s Department of Communication Sciences & Disorders seeks to maintain a qualified applicant pool for adjunct faculty to teach courses and/or provide clinical supervision for graduate students in our state-of-the-art on-campus Clinic. Qualified applicants must hold the equivalent of a Master’s Degree or higher in Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences. Previous university teaching experience preferred. Clinical supervisors must have CCC-SLP (Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology) granted by the American-Speech-Language-Hearing Association (ASHA) and must hold PA licensure as a speech-language pathologist. They should have at least 2-years supervision experience and earned at least two hours of professional development post-certification (one-time requirement) in the area of supervision and/or clinical instruction. For academic courses we are currently seeking instructors with the following areas of expertise: Language Development (undergrad course) Phonetics (undergrad course) Intro to Audiology (undergrad course) American Sign Language (ASL) Interested applicants should send a cover letter and curriculum vitae to Amy Davies, Program Administrator: Amy Davies Center for Communication Sciences & Disorders DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034 Electronic submissions should be emailed to slp@desales.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-english-literature": {
      "title": "Adjunct: English Literature",
      "description": "Adjunct: English Literature. DeSales University's English program, housed in the College of Arts, Education, and Humanities , seeks to maintain a qualified pool of part-time faculty to teach both fully-online-asynchronous and in-person literature courses across the full range of British, American and world literature. Qualified applicants should at minimum have completed an M.A. in English literature or a related field; a Ph.D. is preferred. Must have college-level teaching experience. Applications will be reviewed on a continuing basis as new openings arise. Interested applicants should send a cover letter and curriculum vitae to: Dr. Lisa Wilde English Program DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034 Electronic submissions should be emailed to Lisa.Wilde@desales.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-history-classical-and-european": {
      "title": "Adjunct: History (Classical and European)",
      "description": "Adjunct: History (Classical and European). DeSales University's History program, housed in the College of Arts, Education, and Humanities, seeks to maintain a qualified pool of part-time faculty to teach both fully-online-asynchronous and in-person courses in Classical and European history (Early Modern and Modern). Qualified applicants should at minimum have completed an M.A. in History or a related field; a Ph.D. is preferred. Must have college-level teaching experience. Applications will be reviewed on a continuing basis as new openings arise. Interested applicants should send a cover letter and curriculum vitae to: Dr. Sarah Yu History Program DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034 Electronic submissions should be emailed to Sarah.Yu@desales.edu."
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-master-of-business-administration-mba": {
      "title": "Adjunct: Master of Business Administration (MBA)",
      "description": "Adjunct: Master of Business Administration (MBA). The MBA program seeks to maintain a qualified faculty pool for the following disciplines: Accounting Business Computing Economics Finance Healthcare Management Marketing Teaching formats are online and on-campus/hybrid courses. A Master's degree in the appropriate discipline is required, Ph.D. preferred. Teaching experience using technology also preferred. Please send resumes to: mba@desales.edu"
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-nursing": {
      "title": "Adjunct: Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct: Nursing. DeSales University’s School of Nursing seeks to maintain a qualified applicant pool for adjunct clinical faculty to provide supervision for undergraduate students in our state-of-the-art on-campus labs, as well as within local hospital networks where students attend clinical rotations. Applicants must hold a Master’s Degree or higher in Nursing or must have a BSN and be currently enrolled in an MSN program with a planned completion within 5 years. Previous university teaching experience preferred but not required. Clinical adjunct instructors must hold PA licensure as a Registered Nurse. They should have current or previous bedside experience in the desired specialty area of clinical instruction. For clinical courses we are currently seeking instructors with the following areas of expertise: Pediatrics Labor & Delivery/Mom Baby/NICU/Obstetrics Mental Health Critical Care/ICU Medical Surgical Interested applicants should send a cover letter and curriculum vitae to Sarah Rennalls, Adjunct Faculty Coordinator: Sarah Rennalls College of Healthcare Professions, School of Nursing DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034 Other documentation including RN license, certifications, vaccination status, etc., will be requested upon hire. Electronic submissions should be emailed to nursing@desales.edu"
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-physics": {
      "title": "Adjunct: Physics",
      "description": "Adjunct: Physics. The Department of Chemistry and Physics at DeSales University seeks to maintain a qualified applicant pool for adjunct faculty to teach Physics lecture and laboratory courses as needed. Courses include General Physics (calculus-based) and Introductory Physics (algebra-based). M.S. in Physics or related field is a minimum requirement. Interested applicants should email a cover letter and C.V. to NaturalScience@desales.edu. Or mail to: Ms. Laura Stevens Department of Natural Science DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034"
    },
    "https://www.desales.edu/about/employment#adjunct-philosophy": {
      "title": "Adjunct: Philosophy",
      "description": "Adjunct: Philosophy. DeSales University’s Department of Philosophy & Theology housed in the College of Arts, Education, and Humanities invites applications for a pool of qualified adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate philosophy courses in upcoming semesters on campus in Center Valley, PA. Courses may include introductory surveys, ethics, logic, ancient, modern, or contemporary philosophy. We seek individuals who are committed to the intellectual and spiritual mission of a Catholic, Salesian university. Qualifications Minimum of a master’s degree in Philosophy or a closely related field; ABD or Ph.D. preferred Prior college-level teaching experience is strongly preferred Demonstrated ability to teach philosophical concepts clearly and engagingly Understanding of and respect for the Catholic intellectual tradition and its role within higher education Ability to teach in-person at our Center Valley, PA campus Application Information Candidates should submit the following materials (PDFs preferred): Cover letter indicating your areas of teaching interest/expertise Curriculum vitae Unofficial graduate transcript(s) Contact information for three references Submit materials to: Heather Craft College of Arts, Education & Humanities DeSales University 2755 Station Avenue Center Valley, PA 18034 OR email to: Heather.Craft@desales.edu (subject line: “Adjunct Philosophy Application – [Last Name]”)\" Review of applications will begin immediately and continue on a rolling basis until the pool is filled."
    }
  },
